 "cap": {
  "description": "Cap scenarios. `live` and `tombstones` are the routines stored for the account before the push; `push` lists the pushed routines in order, each `new` (unknown id), `edit` (a live one, still live), `delete` (a live one becomes a tombstone), `revive` (a stored tombstone wins and comes back live) `new_deleted` (a new id pushed with `deleted_at` set: stored as a tombstone, never live, never counts) or `lost_to_tombstone` (a new id that loses last-writer-wins to a stored tombstone: stays deleted, not revived). A push is refused only when it holds a new or revived routine and the live count after the apply is over the limit; `refused` lists the `changes.routines[<i>]` indexes: every other change (deletes included) is counted first, wherever it sits in the array, then the new and revived routines that are live after last-writer-wins (`deleted_at` null) are added one by one in array order, and each one that takes the count past the limit is listed. Pull-only is an empty push.",
